          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: वातायनम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वातायनम् (vātāyanam) — \"a window\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वातायनम् (vātāyanam) is a window, and the word says plainly what a window is for."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is vāta, wind, joined to ayana, a going: a window is the wind's way in. You already say वायुः for wind, and vāta is its near relative from the same root, \"to blow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set it against भित्तिः (bhittiḥ) and the pair makes sense of a room: the wall shuts, the window opens. Neuter, ending in -अम्."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The opening in the wall, named for what comes through it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
