              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सोपानम् (sopānam) — \"a stair\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सोपानम् (sopānam) is a stair, a flight of steps."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The usual way of taking it apart reads it as \"the means of going up\" — a small joining word in front, and behind it the sense of rising. The word carries its purpose on its face, the way वातायनम् (vātāyanam) does."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It stayed home and stayed itself: Hindi and Marathi both keep sopān for a stair. Neuter, ending in -अम्."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The way up, added to the wall and the window."
            }
          ]
        },
