              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्तम्भः (stambhaḥ) — \"a pillar\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्तम्भः (stambhaḥ) is a pillar, a post: the upright that carries a roof."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It rests on stambh, \"to prop, to make firm\". Where भित्तिः (bhittiḥ) splits a space, स्तम्भः (stambhaḥ) holds one open — a wall you can walk past."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English staff and stamp sit near it, and the picture under all three is one thing: something planted hard and standing. Ends in -अः."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What holds the roof up, beside what closes the room in."
            }
          ]
        },
